{"root":{"children":[{"children":[],"direction":null,"format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"This page is part of my ","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"2026 Boulder Colorado Voter Guide","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"link","version":1,"rel":null,"target":null,"title":null,"url":"https://bouldercoloradovoterguide.com/election-guide/"},{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":" for the November 3rd, 2026 General Election in Boulder, Colorado. It covers the Regional Transportation District (RTD) Board of Directors race for District O — the director seat representing Boulder and nearby communities on the board that oversees Denver-area transit service, fares, and long-term planning.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"RTD elected offices are non-partisan, so candidates do not have a party listed next to their name.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"On the ballot (Vote for One): ","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"On the ballot (Vote for One): ","type":"extended-text","version":1},{"detail":0,"format":1,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"Jack Rosenthal","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"I am supporting Jack Rosenthal for Regional Transportation District (RTD) Director - District O. I met Jack last year and have been completely impressed by how he’s embraced improving and transforming RTD. He’s a young, technically-minded person that understands our transit system at a deep level — details about nearly every route in the district, headways, operating costs, labor, accessibility, efficiency challenges, and more.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"children":[{"detail":0,"format":0,"mode":"normal","style":"","text":"But Jack also has a deep understanding of RTD’s big, systemic challenges: how the agency needs to improve trust, increase service in key areas, and how the organization needs to adapt to stay relevant in the face of serious budget challenges in the next few years. Along with RTD-specific work, I appreciate that Jack has been involved with other important state issues — supporting the CoCo Front Range Rail initiative, lending his data analytics skills to helping support the Graduated Income Tax measure (Amendment 87), as well as supporting LGBTQIA+ issues through Hands Off Colorado in opposing Propositions 134 and 135. I really admire younger progressives doing the work and getting things done.","type":"extended-text","version":1}],"direction":"ltr","format":"","indent":0,"type":"paragraph","version":1},{"type":"html","version":1,"html":"<div id=\"yt-rtd-forum\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;max-width:720px;margin:1.5em auto;padding-bottom:56.25%;background:#000;cursor:pointer;overflow:hidden\" data-video-id=\"oZ27AVUmBDc\">\n<img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/oZ27AVUmBDc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"RTD District O candidate forum video\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover\">\n<div style=\"position:absolute;top:50%;left:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%);width:68px;height:48px;background:rgba(33,33,33,.8);border-radius:12px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center\"><